#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:5
#: adb7d3c77dc24d1fb72421ce97d25a88
msgid "OpenDroneID Panel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:7
#: 0eacf5bafadd47c6909fcca56a4617dd
msgid "Mission Planner has a special Drone ID tab in its DATA view for use with OpenDroneID modules attached to the autopilot which allows monitoring status, attaching the required GPS for operator location of the GCS, and UAS and Operator ID string setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:9
#: b7c233674b934d35b953d8c508a8e0b8
msgid "This feature requires Mission Planner 1.3.78 or later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:14
#: f2f76e633c6f4daf905db237471ea0cb
msgid "This control manages the exchange of GCS/Operator information with the RID module, via the AutoPilot connection. If the Drone ID tab does not appear, right click the Data view, select customize, and enable ``tabDroneID``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:18
#: b3ad8c3a60864c46898b062a07fccd96
msgid "GPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:20
#: de18d0913d014947ab398c7b1d01cb83
msgid "Mission Planner must have a source of GPS information about its location. The GPS must provide valid NMEA GPGGA or GNGGA sentences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:22
#: 17c5f800557f470fb8505f962a0217f8
msgid "This can be accomplished by either attaching a GPS to the PC's COM or USB port (some GPS may require an FTDI adapter) or by using an app like `GPS to Bluetooth <https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.cajax.gps2bt2&hl=en_US&gl=US>`__ on your phone to feed GPS data via a Bluetooth serial COM port to Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:27
#: d9c263d57a14485aa4e598f191bc1740
msgid "The COM port and baud rate (normally 9600) are entered in the ``GCS GPS`` dialogs and then Connect to Base GPS pushed. If successful, location data will immediately appear below those dialog boxes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:29
#: d7c8dca3570445ada5435de03e33ed11
msgid "GPS raw output can be viewed in real time by double clicking the GPS status string under the COM Port dropdown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:32
#: 8e38620fb4bd4b19a17fcfd133257981
msgid "Remote ID Status Box"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:34
#: eb4fd046a9fe43638c72168c058d512d
msgid "GCS GPS: Red - Lost Connection to GPS, Orange - Connected, no Fix, Yellow - Fix, no DGPS and Green - DGPS Fix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:35
#: 4e330af7d58f4143aa3c9b4d23917573
msgid "RID Comms: Green - Healthy Connection, Red - Timeout (Currently 5 seconds)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:36
#: aa2aa9ec6cd740ef833d16e0d92006db
msgid "ARM Status: Green when Armed, Otherwise Red with Reason in RID Armed Status Reason in Status tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:37
#: 48ab11f634df4437a29052bcdb148d62
msgid "UAS ID: Red when the UAS ID tab is not fully populated. Typically, this information will be provided by the RID module when using Standard ID, and may be populated by the user in future implementation of after-market or add-on RemoteID Broadcast Modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:40
#: bad814423ccf47ffa19c2e269bc9945e
msgid "String Setup Tabs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:42
#: 5d69dca0cca4483d87027dec8c111e5c
msgid "Two tabs are provided for input of UAS and Operator information in these initial test and development version of the interface. Some of these may become read-only and obtained from the RemoteID module in the future, depending on jurisdiction and implementation. They are provided for experimentation and testing initially."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:45
#: 6257a13772b84f16b1fc26dfcd637e22
msgid "Master Status Indicator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:46
#: 55d4bc54f43d452d9a363da0c3191c7d
msgid "Located in the left middle side of the panel. The master status will indicate RED if any conditions for proper operation are not valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/opendroneid.rst:48
#: 6d4980be28cf49459ee47dbb76b20d23
msgid "Local regulations may require such a master indicator. In Mission Planner, this will be present in this tab as well as on the map (pending)."
msgstr ""
